{"id": "EUVD-2026-82082", "enisaUuid": "6de6558d-7d2f-3090-bcfd-613f46b44b18", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nPCI: Fix UAF when probe runs concurrent to dyn ID removal\n\nDynamic IDs are only guaranteed to be valid when dynids.lock is held,\nas remove_id_store() can free the node. Thus, make a copy in\npci_match_device(). Also, clarify that the id parameter is only valid\nduring probe.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:09:45", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:51:34", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d867db0a2602919510f346bc555f7b3093f6b6cc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2cbcb0819c6367e1d5b0792a960594cc19576e23", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c36816feff47f676dcc51919777d483f4146c1ee", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/42a5661ff7e4c7d3c5025d0f8e5079fb5479ea49", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3ffc4c9690c33ee28cdb3d0182b12f9c623e3acc"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90421", "GHSA-286w-pmvg-5rp9"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "15b8d4db-92ad-3b73-a97b-b42eab2a238c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "1c40b939-e97c-3537-bbf9-2fcf95f362da", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "213dee1e-6cda-3edb-9560-4ecfe5b96a36", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "2ba58909-e538-31da-a844-d8d3d3804a4b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0994375e9614f78657031e04e30019b9cdb62795 <c36816feff47f676dcc51919777d483f4146c1ee"}, {"id": "3786de5f-14d1-36be-9bcb-c8ff060195f5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "388c30b6-1f73-3848-b7b2-48353ad4fc5d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0994375e9614f78657031e04e30019b9cdb62795 <d86